    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15000#pullrequestreview-5660582771\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks for this!</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635205995,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793058431
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15000#discussion_r4383704838\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For this it'll actually want to define the <code>run</code> function as <code>async</code>. While Wasmtime will allow this as-is and run it, the component model will dynamically trap should <code>run</code> call the imported <code>log</code> function or otherwise attempt to block. Basically sync component-model functions can't block, so a sync <code>run</code> function here isn't too useful</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635205996,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793058431
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15000#discussion_r4383709599\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One option to avoid this if you'd like is to use <a href=\"https://docs.rs/wasmtime/latest/wasmtime/component/struct.HasSelf.html\"><code>HasSelf</code></a></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635205997,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793058431
    },
    {
