    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> asteurer submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15000#pullrequestreview-5660798687\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635213498,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793060334
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> asteurer created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15000#discussion_r4383889993\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh, interesting. I added a <code>tokio::time::sleep</code> to the host's impl of <code>log</code> just now and it does indeed trap. I think I'm misunderstanding the assertion that the <a href=\"https://github.com/WebAssembly/component-model/blob/main/design/mvp/Concurrency.md#summary\">Concurrency Explainer</a> makes:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Thus</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">overall</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">async</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WIT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Component</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Model</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">behave</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">like</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"color\"</span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"p\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>How can WIT be considered \"colorless\" when an export is required to be <code>async</code> in order to call an <code>async</code> import?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635213499,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793060334
    },
